# Windows Event ID Cheat Sheet (SOC Analyst Project)

I created a structured cheat sheet of the most critical Windows Event IDs used in SOC monitoring and incident detection.

   Key Event IDs Covered
4624 – Successful logon (used for tracking account access)
4625 – Failed logon attempts (brute force detection)
4688 – Process creation (malware execution monitoring)
4104 – PowerShell script execution (fileless attack detection)
4720 – User account creation (persistence detection)
4728 – Privileged group membership changes (privilege escalation)
7045 – New service installed (persistence technique)
1102 – Security logs cleared (defense evasion)
4769 – Kerberos service ticket requests (Kerberoasting detection)

   Skills Demonstrated
Windows event log analysis
Threat detection mapping
SOC monitoring fundamentals
Understanding of attacker techniques (MITRE-style thinking)

